duckling (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Writes ODS, ODP and XLSX as well as ODT and DOCX, each offered for the
    document it is a sibling of: ODS when every file in the queue is XLSX,
    XLSX when they are all ODS, ODP when they are all PPTX. A book converted
    to a spreadsheet is one empty sheet and a list of what was dropped, so it
    is not offered. The slide leg is one-way, because waddle writes ODP and
    no PPTX.
  * Text layer only, a checkbox for a PDF that already has text in it. Clean
    Code, 460 pages, takes 179 seconds through the models and 1.2 seconds
    from its text layer. What it gives up is the headings, the tables and any
    page that needs OCR. A file with no text layer at all says so rather than
    coming back blank.
  * A line no longer falls out of a paragraph. On a PDF, roughly every few
    paragraphs, one line was dropped from the paragraph it belonged to and
    written after it, splicing the sentence it left behind. Found from this
    application's own output and fixed upstream; documents are read by
    docling.rs 1.51 now.
  * The install is about 230 MB smaller and nothing converts differently for
    it. Three of the table-structure model files were variants docling.rs
    never opened, because one it prefers ships beside them, and that encoder
    is a further 118 MB smaller than the file that shipped before, the same
    model with padding stripped out of it upstream. 575 MB installed.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:16:22 -0500

duckling (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * German. Duckling comes up in German on a machine set to German — the
    toolbar, the queue, the preview and every line the status bar shows —
    reading the language the desktop already knows, with nothing to choose and
    English for any other. What a file is stays as the file says it: the format
    a row was read as, the extensions docling.rs does not read, and the names
    of most output formats are not translated, DOCX and JSON being DOCX and
    JSON in any language.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 22:04:49 -0500

duckling (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Writes ODT and DOCX as well, through waddle: a plain, well-structured
    office document from what docling.rs read, with the pictures inside the
    package. What the package could not hold is listed on the result.
  * Reads with docling.rs 1.37.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 22:12:34 -0500

duckling (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First packaged build. A window that converts Word, PowerPoint, Excel,
    PDF, HTML, EPUB and some forty other formats into DocLang, Markdown,
    docling JSON, a DocLang archive or LaTeX, in batches, with the output
    beside each file or in one folder and never over an existing file. The
    layout, table and OCR models for PDFs and scans ship in the package.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 23:30:00 -0500
